+---
+id: task-004-rent-equipment-by-the-hour
+type: task
+title: "Rent equipment by the hour"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Rent equipment by the hour
+
+## Goal
+
+Visitors who only want a board for an afternoon can rent it by the hour, instead of being turned away.
+
+## Scope
+
+Changes `src/index.ts`, used by `addEquipment`, `quote`, `book` and `availability`:
+
+- `addEquipment` also accepts `hourlyPrice`, the price in euro cents of one hour of rental. It is optional. When
+  given, it must be a non-negative integer, as `dailyPrice` is (task-001 AC8).
+- A rental shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour is priced at the item's `hourlyPrice` for each
+  hour: hours times `hourlyPrice`. Example: 3 hours at 1000 cents is 3000.
+- An item without an `hourlyPrice` cannot be rented by the hour: `quote` and `book` throw for such a period.
+- `quote` and `book` return the hourly total. `book` returns the same total as `quote` for the same period.
+- `availability` accepts an hourly period, with the same period rules as `quote` (see rule 2). It does not need an
+  hourly price, because it reports only whether items are free.
+
+## Rules
+
+1. Money is an integer number of euro cents (task-001 rule 1).
+2. Times are UTC, written as ISO-8601 strings with a `Z` suffix. A period is one of two kinds:
+   - a rental of a day or more: starts and ends at midnight UTC, as before (task-001 rules 2 and 3);
+   - a rental shorter than a day: starts and ends on the hour UTC, for example `2026-07-01T09:00:00Z`. Minutes and
+     seconds must be zero.
+   A period whose end is not after its start is rejected, as before. A period that starts or ends off the hour, or
+   runs for a day or more without midnight at both ends, is rejected.
+3. This task supersedes task-001 rule 3 for rentals shorter than a day that start and end on the hour: their total
+   is hours times `hourlyPrice`, not days times `dailyPrice`. Rentals of a day or more keep the task-001 and
+   task-003 totals.
+4. The same item cannot be booked twice for overlapping periods, as before (task-001 rule 4). Hourly periods use the
+   same half-open overlap check, so a booking ending at 10:00 does not clash with one starting at 10:00.
+5. The 10% long-rental discount of task-003 applies only to rentals of 3 days or more, so it never applies to an
+   hourly rental.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC1: `addEquipment` accepts an item with an `hourlyPrice` that is a non-negative integer, and an item without one.
+  It rejects an `hourlyPrice` that is negative, fractional or not a number (the same checks as `dailyPrice`).
+- AC2: A rental shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour quotes hours times `hourlyPrice` (e.g. 09:00 to
+  12:00 at 1000 is 3000).
+- AC3: A rental of exactly one hour quotes the `hourlyPrice`; a rental of 23 hours across midnight quotes 23 times it.
+- AC4: `book` returns the same hourly total as `quote` for the same period, and records the booking.
+- AC5: `quote` and `book` throw for an hourly period on an item that has no `hourlyPrice`, and `book` records nothing
+  when it throws.
+- AC6: `quote` and `book` throw for an hourly-shaped period that starts or ends off the hour (e.g. 09:30), and for a
+  period of a day or more that does not run midnight to midnight (e.g. 09:00 one day to 09:00 the next).
+- AC7: Two hourly bookings for the same item that only touch (one ends at the hour the other starts) are both accepted;
+  an overlapping one throws.
+- AC8: `availability` lists an item free for an hourly period, and leaves it out when an overlapping booking exists,
+  whether or not the item has an `hourlyPrice`.
+- AC9: A rental of a whole day or more is priced as before: task-001 and task-003 totals are unchanged. Existing
+  error behaviour not covered by this task is unchanged.
+
+## Notes
+
+- No runtime dependency is added. Tests use `node --test` (the existing `test` script).
+- Each acceptance criterion gets at least one happy-path test and one edge- or error-path test.
+- Tests that asserted the old rule that a start or end off midnight is always rejected are updated where it now
+  differs: an item with an `hourlyPrice` accepts an on-the-hour period, and an item without one still throws.
+- Cancellation remains out of scope, as in task-001.
+
+## Build record
+
+- Red first: ten new or updated tests failed on the unchanged module (the hourly price was not accepted, and an
+  on-the-hour period was rejected), before any change to `src/index.ts`.
+- Implementation in `src/index.ts`: `addEquipment` takes an optional `hourlyPrice`; `parsePeriod` accepts on-the-hour
+  UTC instants and marks a period shorter than a day as hourly; `priceOf` prices an hourly period at hours times
+  `hourlyPrice`, and throws for an item without one. `book` prices the period before it records the booking, so a
+  throw books nothing.
+- Tests updated where the old rule differs: the off-midnight start tests now use 09:30, which stays rejected for any
+  item, and an hourly rental of an item without an hourly price still throws.
+- `npm test`: 49 of 49 pass.
+- Not run: no type checker or linter is installed in this repository; `tsc` and an ESLint run were not available.
